config BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_CO5300_175
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3 1.75\" Round AMOLED (CO5300 466x466)"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    help
        The Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75" board: a 466x466 round
        AMOLED on a CO5300 controller over QSPI. Same pixel grid and UI
        as the 1.43" profile, but CO5300-only (no SH8601 fallback) and
        different GPIO pins. The AXP2101 PMIC's power rails are left at the
        board's defaults; its battery telemetry is read (read-only) for
        the UI battery indicator (axp2101.c). Links against the same
        `esp_lcd_sh8601` managed component (it frames QSPI for the whole
        SH8601/CO5300 family).

# Demo + burn-in options below reuse the same CONFIG symbol names as the
# amoled_sh8601 (1.43") profile. The two profiles are mutually exclusive
# (selected via the BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY choice), so at most one definition
# of each symbol is ever visible — and the defaults are identical — so
# the shared adapter/main.c code reads one consistent set of values
# regardless of which AMOLED board is built. This board has a QMI8658
# IMU (like the 1.43"), so the motion-wake and auto-rotate options apply.

config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DEMO
    bool "AMOLED driver-verification demo (no Wi-Fi, static test pattern)"
    default n
    depends on BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_CO5300_175
    help
        When enabled, app_main bypasses NVS / Wi-Fi / HTTP / NTP entirely
        and just renders a static test pattern (color bars + corner
        markers + centre crosshair) on the AMOLED. Use this to verify
        the CO5300 panel driver: SLPOUT/DISPON, RGB565 byte order, and
        the CASET/RASET column/row gap. Disable for normal builds.

menu "AMOLED burn-in mitigation"
    depends on BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_CO5300_175

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_DIM_MINUTES
        int "Minutes of idle before dimming the panel"
        default 2
        range 1 60
        help
            After this many minutes with no activity event (button or
            qualifying POST /summary push) the burn-in adapter dims the
            panel from BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT down to
            BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DIMMED_BRIGHTNESS_PCT.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_OFF_MINUTES
        int "Minutes of idle before turning the panel off"
        default 5
        range 1 240
        help
            After this many minutes idle the burn-in adapter issues
            DISPOFF (MIPI DCS 0x28). The HTTP server keeps running so
            an incoming push wakes the panel within ~200 ms. Must be
            >= BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_DIM_MINUTES; equal values mean
            "no dim phase, jump straight to off."

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT
        int "Active-state brightness, % of panel maximum"
        default 70
        range 0 100
        help
            Brightness used in the ACTIVE state, as a percentage of the
            CO5300 0x51 register's 8-bit range. The 70 % default matches
            the catalog's recommended luminance cap.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DIMMED_BRIGHTNESS_PCT
        int "Dimmed-state brightness, % of panel maximum"
        default 20
        range 0 100
        help
            Brightness used in the DIMMED state. Should be <=
            BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT. Set to 0 to make
            the dim phase visually identical to off (panel still
            powered).

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_WAKE_FADE_MS
        int "Brightness fade-up duration (ms)"
        default 300
        range 0 5000
        help
            Duration of the linear brightness ramp when the panel is
            waking or transitioning to a brighter state. The CO5300 has
            no hardware fade primitive, so the adapter writes intermediate
            0x51 register values at ~30 Hz over this interval. Set to 0
            for instantaneous wake.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_SLEEP_FADE_MS
        int "Brightness fade-down duration (ms)"
        default 1500
        range 0 5000
        help
            Duration of the linear brightness ramp when the panel is
            dimming or powering down. For DIMMED->OFF transitions the
            DISPOFF command runs after the fade reaches 0. Set to 0 for
            instantaneous dim/off.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_MOTION_THRESHOLD_MG
        int "Motion-wake threshold (milli-g)"
        default 50
        range 1 2000
        help
            Per-sample accelerometer delta-magnitude (mg) that the
            QMI8658 sampler treats as motion. Above this, the burn-in
            adapter posts EV_MOTION and the panel wakes from dim/off.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ORIENTATION_AUTO
        bool "Auto-rotate the UI to follow the device's orientation"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, a background task samples the QMI8658
            accelerometer and rotates the LVGL display in 90°
            quadrants to match the gravity vector. Disable for
            diagnostic builds that need a fixed orientation; the
            burn-in adapter's motion-wake path stays active either way.

endmenu
